        text: "One of the primary advantages of asset-based lending is its ability to convert balance sheet assets into immediate, scalable working capital. Unlike traditional term loans, asset-based facilities are underwritten primarily on receivable quality and collateral performance, enabling faster access to capital through revolving credit structures. This liquidity supports uninterrupted operations, working capital stability, and disciplined cash management during periods of growth or volatility, reinforcing liquidity predictability across operating cycles.",
