              "text": "Accounts payable and accounts receivable are closely connected in healthcare financial management. Accounts receivable refers to the money owed to a healthcare provider for services delivered but not yet paid for, while accounts payable represent the bills and obligations the provider must pay to suppliers, vendors, and staff."
