      "title": "Is a Purchase Order a Contract in Business Transactions?",
      "description": "In business transactions, a purchase order (PO) is a document issued by a buyer to confirm the intent to purchase goods or services. It specifies details such as quantity, price, and delivery terms, m",
      "metaTitle": "Is a Purchase Order a Contract? EPOCH Financial",
      "metaDescription": "Is a purchase order a contract? Understand its legal role in business transactions and how it protects both buyers and suppliers.",
