              "text": "The efficiency of this cycle has a direct impact on accounts receivable and cash flow. When customers pay promptly, cash flows back into the business quickly, allowing companies to cover expenses, pay suppliers, and reinvest in operations. A shorter cycle strengthens liquidity and ensures that working capital is readily available."
